# evaluation. Committing the files would redistribute a licensed commercial
# typeface, and deploying them would publish it. Both are licence breaches.
#
# Consequences, all intended:
#   - a fresh clone has no Eiko and renders the fallback stack declared in
#     src/styles/fonts.css
#   - CI and every production build do the same
#   - to see Eiko locally, copy the .otf files from the trial package into
#     public/assets/fonts/ (see README)
#
# Remove this rule only after a licence is purchased, and then commit the
# licensed woff2 rather than these trial .otf files.
public/assets/fonts/PPEiko*

